{"code":"ar","name":"Arabic","native":"العربية","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A1","pronunciation":[{"t":"ع (ayn) is a deep throaty sound","r":"ʿa","tip":"Tighten your throat like swallowing in reverse: عَرب (ʿarab) = Arab."},{"t":"ح (ḥa) is a breathy deep H","r":"ḥa","tip":"Breathe hard from deep in the throat: حَب (ḥabb) = love."},{"t":"خ (kha) scrapes like clearing your throat","r":"kha","tip":"Like Scottish LOCH: خُبز (khubz) = bread."},{"t":"ق (qaf) is a deep K from the back","r":"qa","tip":"K made far back in the throat: قَلب (qalb) = heart."},{"t":"ث and ذ are soft TH sounds","r":"tha / dha","tip":"ث like THINK (ثلاثة = three), ذ like THIS (ذهب = gold)."}],"alphabet":{"title":"The Arabic alphabet","explain":"Arabic has 28 letters, written right-to-left. Letters change shape at the start, middle and end of words — but the sounds stay the same. Learn sounds first, shapes second!","letters":[{"t":"ا","r":"a (alif)"},{"t":"ب","r":"b (ba)"},{"t":"ت","r":"t (ta)"},{"t":"ث","r":"th as in think (tha)"},{"t":"ج","r":"j (jim)"},{"t":"ح","r":"ḥ - deep breathy h (ḥa)"},{"t":"خ","r":"kh - throaty (kha)"},{"t":"د","r":"d (dal)"},{"t":"ذ","r":"dh as in this (dhal)"},{"t":"ر","r":"rolled r (ra)"},{"t":"ز","r":"z (zay)"},{"t":"س","r":"s (sin)"},{"t":"ش","r":"sh (shin)"},{"t":"ص","r":"ṣ - deep s (ṣad)"},{"t":"ض","r":"ḍ - deep d (ḍad)"},{"t":"ط","r":"ṭ - deep t (ṭa)"},{"t":"ظ","r":"ẓ - deep z (ẓa)"},{"t":"ع","r":"ʿ - throaty ayn (ayn)"},{"t":"غ","r":"gh - throaty (ghayn)"},{"t":"ف","r":"f (fa)"},{"t":"ق","r":"q - deep k (qaf)"},{"t":"ك","r":"k (kaf)"},{"t":"ل","r":"l (lam)"},{"t":"م","r":"m (mim)"},{"t":"ن","r":"n (nun)"},{"t":"ه","r":"h (ha)"},{"t":"و","r":"w (waw)"},{"t":"ي","r":"y (ya)"}]},"counting":{"title":"Counting 0 to 100","explain":"Numbers 1–10 first, then 11–19 (ones + عشر), then tens to 100. 21 = واحد وعشرون (one and twenty) — ones come FIRST!","numbers":[{"t":"صفر","r":"ṣifr","en":"0"},{"t":"واحد","r":"wāḥid","en":"1"},{"t":"اثنان","r":"ithnān","en":"2"},{"t":"ثلاثة","r":"thalātha","en":"3"},{"t":"أربعة","r":"arbaʿa","en":"4"},{"t":"خمسة","r":"khamsa","en":"5"},{"t":"ستة","r":"sitta","en":"6"},{"t":"سبعة","r":"sabʿa","en":"7"},{"t":"ثمانية","r":"thamāniya","en":"8"},{"t":"تسعة","r":"tisʿa","en":"9"},{"t":"عشرة","r":"ʿashara","en":"10"},{"t":"أحد عشر","r":"aḥada ʿashar","en":"11"},{"t":"اثنا عشر","r":"ithnā ʿashar","en":"12"},{"t":"ثلاثة عشر","r":"thalāthata ʿashar","en":"13"},{"t":"أربعة عشر","r":"arbaʿata ʿashar","en":"14"},{"t":"خمسة عشر","r":"khamsata ʿashar","en":"15"},{"t":"ستة عشر","r":"sittata ʿashar","en":"16"},{"t":"سبعة عشر","r":"sabʿata ʿashar","en":"17"},{"t":"ثمانية عشر","r":"thamāniyata ʿashar","en":"18"},{"t":"تسعة عشر","r":"tisʿata ʿashar","en":"19"},{"t":"عشرون","r":"ʿishrūn","en":"20"},{"t":"ثلاثون","r":"thalāthūn","en":"30"},{"t":"أربعون","r":"arbaʿūn","en":"40"},{"t":"خمسون","r":"khamsūn","en":"50"},{"t":"ستون","r":"sittūn","en":"60"},{"t":"سبعون","r":"sabʿūn","en":"70"},{"t":"ثمانون","r":"thamānūn","en":"80"},{"t":"تسعون","r":"tisʿūn","en":"90"},{"t":"مائة","r":"miʾa","en":"100"}],"rules":["11–19 = ones + عشر: ثلاثة عشر = 13.","21+ puts ones FIRST: واحد وعشرون = 21 (one-and-twenty). Tens end in -ون: عشرون، ثلاثون."]},"level":{"title":"Starter: greetings, gender, first verbs","goals":["Greet people and introduce yourself","Know gender, plurals and numbers","Use present verbs and say 'I have'"],"units":[{"id":"A1-U1","title":"First words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U1-L1","title":"Greetings: السلام عليكم","learn":"The famous greeting! السلام عليكم (peace upon you) → answer وعليكم السلام (and upon you peace). Morning: صباح الخير → answer صباح النور! Greetings always come in PAIRS.","vocab":[{"t":"السلام عليكم","r":"as-salāmu ʿalaykum","en":"peace upon you (hello)","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"وعليكم السلام","r":"wa ʿalaykum as-salām","en":"and upon you peace (reply)","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"مرحبا","r":"marḥaban","en":"hello","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"صباح الخير","r":"ṣabāḥ al-khayr","en":"good morning","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"مساء الخير","r":"masāʾ al-khayr","en":"good evening","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"شكرا","r":"shukran","en":"thanks","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"عفوا","r":"ʿafwan","en":"you're welcome / excuse me","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"مع السلامة","r":"maʿa as-salāma","en":"goodbye","pos":"phrase"}],"grammar":{"title":"Greetings come in pairs","explain":"السلام عليكم → وعليكم السلام. صباح الخير → صباح النور (morning of light!). مساء الخير → مساء النور. Never answer a greeting with the same greeting — use its PAIR!","pattern":"greeting → pair-answer","examples":[{"t":"السلام عليكم!","r":"as-salāmu ʿalaykum!","en":"Peace upon you!"},{"t":"وعليكم السلام!","r":"wa ʿalaykum as-salām!","en":"And upon you peace!"},{"t":"صباح الخير! — صباح النور!","r":"ṣabāḥ al-khayr! — ṣabāḥ an-nūr!","en":"Good morning! — Morning of light!"}],"mistakes":["Answering السلام عليكم with السلام عليكم — reply وعليكم السلام!","Saying صباح الخير at night — evenings need مساء الخير!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"ليلى","t":"السلام عليكم!","r":"as-salāmu ʿalaykum!","en":"Peace upon you!"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"وعليكم السلام! صباح الخير!","r":"wa ʿalaykum as-salām! ṣabāḥ al-khayr!","en":"And upon you peace! Good morning!"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"صباح النور! شكرا!","r":"ṣabāḥ an-nūr! shukran!","en":"Morning of light! Thanks!"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"عفوا! مع السلامة!","r":"ʿafwan! maʿa as-salāma!","en":"You're welcome! Goodbye!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Peace upon you!","answer":"السلام عليكم!"},{"type":"fill","q":"صباح ___! (morning reply: light)","answer":"النور"},{"type":"choose","q":"Reply to السلام عليكم is…","options":["السلام عليكم","وعليكم السلام","صباح الخير","مع السلامة"],"answer":"وعليكم السلام"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: عليكم / السلام","answer":"السلام عليكم"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: السلام عليكم!","answer":"السلام عليكم!"}],"quiz":[{"q":"Reply to السلام عليكم is…","options":["same greeting","وعليكم السلام","شكرا","مرحبا"],"answer":1,"why":"Greetings come in pairs!"},{"q":"صباح النور is…","options":["good evening","morning reply","goodbye","thanks"],"answer":1,"why":"Pairs with صباح الخير."},{"q":"شكرا means…","options":["please","thanks","hello","goodbye"],"answer":1,"why":"شكرا = thanks."},{"q":"عفوا means…","options":["sorry only","you're welcome / excuse me","yes","hello"],"answer":1,"why":"عفوا does double duty."},{"q":"مع السلامة is…","options":["hello","goodbye","thanks","please"],"answer":1,"why":"مع السلامة = go with safety."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Greetings worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["peace upon you","thanks","goodbye"],"key":["السلام عليكم","شكرا","مع السلامة"]},{"instruction":"Give the pair-answer.","items":["السلام عليكم → …","صباح الخير → …","مساء الخير → …"],"key":["وعليكم السلام","صباح النور","مساء النور"]},{"instruction":"Morning chat.","items":["Good morning!","Morning of light!"],"key":["صباح الخير","صباح النور"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U1-L2","title":"Names and how are you","learn":"اسمي ليلى = My name is Layla. Ask: ما اسمك؟ (m) / ما اسمكِ؟ (f) — -KA for men, -KI for women! How are you: كيف حالك؟ → بخير، الحمد لله (fine, praise God)!","vocab":[{"t":"ما اسمك","r":"mā ismuk / ismukī","en":"what is your name","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"اسمي","r":"ismī","en":"my name is","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"كيف حالك","r":"kayfa ḥāluk / ḥāluki","en":"how are you","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"بخير","r":"bikhayr","en":"fine / well","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"الحمد لله","r":"al-ḥamdu lillāh","en":"praise God","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"وأنت","r":"wa anta / anti","en":"and you","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"من فضلك","r":"min faḍlik","en":"please","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"نعم / لا","r":"naʿam / lā","en":"yes / no","pos":"phrase"}],"grammar":{"title":"-ka (m) / -ki (f): your","explain":"اسمكَ (ismuka) = your name (to a man), اسمكِ (ismukī) = your name (to a woman). حالكَ/حالكِ the same. اسمي = MY name (works for everyone). Check who you talk to — pick -KA or -KI!","pattern":"-ka (to men) · -ki (to women)","examples":[{"t":"ما اسمك؟ (to Omar)","r":"mā ismuk?","en":"What is your name? (m)"},{"t":"ما اسمكِ؟ (to Layla)","r":"mā ismukī?","en":"What is your name? (f)"},{"t":"اسمي ليلى.","r":"ismī laylā.","en":"My name is Layla."}],"mistakes":["Saying اسمك to a woman — women get اسمكِ (-KI)!","Forgetting الحمد لله after بخير — it always follows!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"عمر","t":"ما اسمكِ؟","r":"mā ismukī?","en":"What is your name? (to f)"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"اسمي ليلى. ما اسمك؟","r":"ismī laylā. mā ismuk?","en":"My name is Layla. What is yours? (to m)"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"اسمي عمر. كيف حالكِ؟","r":"ismī ʿumar. kayfa ḥāluki?","en":"My name is Omar. How are you? (to f)"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"بخير، الحمد لله!","r":"bikhayr, al-ḥamdu lillāh!","en":"Fine, praise God!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: My name is Layla","answer":"اسمي ليلى"},{"type":"fill","q":"بخير، ___! (praise God)","answer":"الحمد لله"},{"type":"choose","q":"'What is your name?' to a WOMAN is…","options":["ما اسمك؟","ما اسمكِ؟","ما اسمي؟","ما اسمه؟"],"answer":"ما اسمكِ؟"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: ليلى / اسمي","answer":"اسمي ليلى"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: اسمي عمر.","answer":"اسمي عمر."}],"quiz":[{"q":"-KI ending is for…","options":["men","women","plural","formal"],"answer":1,"why":"اسمكِ = your (f) name."},{"q":"اسمي works for…","options":["men only","women only","everyone","plural"],"answer":2,"why":"اسمي = my name, all speakers."},{"q":"الحمد لله means…","options":["thank you","praise God","good luck","welcome"],"answer":1,"why":"Always follows بخير."},{"q":"كيف حالك؟ means…","options":["what is this","how are you","where are you","who are you"],"answer":1,"why":"كيف حالك = how are you."},{"q":"من فضلك means…","options":["thanks","please","sorry","hello"],"answer":1,"why":"من فضلك = please."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Names worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["my name is","how are you","please"],"key":["اسمي","كيف حالك","من فضلك"]},{"instruction":"-ka or -ki?","items":["your name (to Omar)","your name (to Layla)"],"key":["ما اسمك؟","ما اسمكِ؟"]},{"instruction":"Meet someone.","items":["My name is Omar","Fine, praise God!"],"key":["اسمي عمر","بخير، الحمد لله"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U2","title":"Gender and plurals","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U2-L1","title":"Gender: هذا / هذه","learn":"Two genders! هذا = this (m), هذه = this (f). Feminine usually ends in ة (ta marbuta): مدرسة (school-f), سيارة (car-f). No ة? Usually masculine: كتاب (book-m), بيت (house-m)!","vocab":[{"t":"هذا","r":"hādhā","en":"this (m)","pos":"pronoun"},{"t":"هذه","r":"hādhihī","en":"this (f)","pos":"pronoun"},{"t":"رجل","r":"rajul","en":"man","pos":"noun"},{"t":"امرأة","r":"imraʾa","en":"woman","pos":"noun"},{"t":"ولد","r":"walad","en":"boy","pos":"noun"},{"t":"بنت","r":"bint","en":"girl","pos":"noun"},{"t":"كبير","r":"kabīr","en":"big (m)","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"صغير","r":"ṣaghīr","en":"small (m)","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"هذا (m) / هذه (f) + ة","explain":"هذا كتاب (this is a book-m), هذه مدرسة (this is a school-f). Adjectives match: رجل كبير (big man), امرأة كبيرة (big woman) — feminine adds ة!","pattern":"هذا + m · هذه + f (ة)","examples":[{"t":"هذا كتاب.","r":"hādhā kitāb.","en":"This is a book."},{"t":"هذه مدرسة.","r":"hādhihī madrasa.","en":"This is a school."},{"t":"امرأة كبيرة.","r":"imraʾa kabīra.","en":"A big woman."}],"mistakes":["Saying هذا مدرسة — ة-words need هذه!","Saying امرأة كبير — feminine needs كبيرة!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"ليلى","t":"هل هذا كتاب؟","r":"hal hādhā kitāb?","en":"Is this a book?"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"نعم، هذا كتاب كبير.","r":"naʿam, hādhā kitāb kabīr.","en":"Yes, this is a big book."},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"وهذه مدرسة؟","r":"wa hādhihī madrasa?","en":"And is this a school?"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"نعم! هذه مدرسة صغيرة.","r":"naʿam! hādhihī madrasa ṣaghīra.","en":"Yes! This is a small school."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This is a book","answer":"هذا كتاب"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ مدرسة. (This, f)","answer":"هذه"},{"type":"choose","q":"'A big woman' is…","options":["امرأة كبير","امرأة كبيرة","امرأة الكبير","الكبيرة امرأة"],"answer":"امرأة كبيرة"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: كتاب / هذا","answer":"هذا كتاب"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: هذا كتاب كبير.","answer":"هذا كتاب كبير."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ة (ta marbuta) marks…","options":["masculine","feminine","plural","past"],"answer":1,"why":"مدرسة، سيارة — feminine!."},{"q":"هذا is for…","options":["feminine","masculine","plural","all"],"answer":1,"why":"هذا كتاب — masculine this."},{"q":"امرأة كبيرة matches because…","options":["both plural","both feminine","both big","both new"],"answer":1,"why":"Adjectives match gender."},{"q":"بنت means…","options":["boy","girl","man","woman"],"answer":1,"why":"بنت = girl."},{"q":"كبير means…","options":["small","big","new","old"],"answer":1,"why":"كبير = big (m)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Gender worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["this (m)","this (f)","girl"],"key":["هذا","هذه","بنت"]},{"instruction":"هذا or هذه?","items":["… كتاب","… مدرسة","… سيارة"],"key":["هذا","هذه","هذه"]},{"instruction":"Match adjectives.","items":["a big book","a small school"],"key":["كتاب كبير","مدرسة صغيرة"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U2-L2","title":"Plurals: كتاب → كتب","learn":"Plurals transform! Sound feminine: سيارة → سيارات (add -ات). People masculine: مدرس → مدرسون (-ون). And BROKEN plurals reshape the word: كتاب → كتب, قلم → أقلام. Learn each word WITH its plural!","vocab":[{"t":"كتاب","r":"kitāb","en":"book","pos":"noun"},{"t":"كتب","r":"kutub","en":"books","pos":"noun"},{"t":"قلم","r":"qalam","en":"pen","pos":"noun"},{"t":"سيارة","r":"sayyāra","en":"car","pos":"noun"},{"t":"بيت","r":"bayt","en":"house","pos":"noun"},{"t":"مدرسة","r":"madrasa","en":"school","pos":"noun"},{"t":"كثير","r":"kathīr","en":"many / a lot","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"قليل","r":"qalīl","en":"few / little","pos":"adverb"}],"grammar":{"title":"Three plural roads","explain":"سيارة→سيارات (-ات for most feminine). مدرس→مدرسون (-ون for male people). Broken: كتاب→كتب, قلم→أقلام, بيت→بيوت — memorise the pair!","pattern":"-ات · -ون · broken (كتب)","examples":[{"t":"سيارات كثيرة.","r":"sayyārāt kathīra.","en":"Many cars."},{"t":"عندي كتب.","r":"ʿindī kutub.","en":"I have books."},{"t":"أقلام قليلة.","r":"aqlām qalīla.","en":"Few pens."}],"mistakes":["Saying كتابات — books are broken: كتب!","Saying مدرسات for male teachers — men take -ون!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"عمر","t":"كم كتابا عندك؟","r":"kam kitāban ʿindak?","en":"How many books do you have?"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"عندي كتب كثيرة!","r":"ʿindī kutub kathīra!","en":"I have many books!"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"وأقلام؟","r":"wa aqlām?","en":"And pens?"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"أقلام قليلة.","r":"aqlām qalīla.","en":"Few pens."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I have books","answer":"عندي كتب"},{"type":"fill","q":"سيارة → ___ (plural)","answer":"سيارات"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Books' (plural of كتاب) is…","options":["كتابات","كتب","كتابون","كتابين"],"answer":"كتب"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: كتب / عندي","answer":"عندي كتب"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: عندي كتب كثيرة!","answer":"عندي كتب كثيرة!"}],"quiz":[{"q":"كتاب → plural is…","options":["كتابات","كتب","كتابون","كتابين"],"answer":1,"why":"Broken plural: كتب."},{"q":"سيارة → plural is…","options":["سيارات","سيارون","سير","سيارةون"],"answer":0,"why":"Feminine sound plural -ات."},{"q":"Broken plurals…","options":["add -ون","reshape the word","add -ات","double letters"],"answer":1,"why":"كتاب→كتب — reshaped!"},{"q":"كثير means…","options":["few","many","all","some"],"answer":1,"why":"كثير = many/a lot."},{"q":"قليل means…","options":["many","few","none","more"],"answer":1,"why":"قليل = few/little."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Plurals worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["books","car","many"],"key":["كتب","سيارة","كثير"]},{"instruction":"Make plurals.","items":["كتاب → …","سيارة → …","قلم → …"],"key":["كتب","سيارات","أقلام"]},{"instruction":"Count things.","items":["I have many books!","Few pens"],"key":["عندي كتب كثيرة","أقلام قليلة"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U3","title":"First verbs","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U3-L1","title":"Present tense: أنا أدرس","learn":"Verbs wear PREFIXES! أدرس (I study), تدرس (you-m study), يدرس (he studies), تدرس (she studies), ندرس (we study). One verb, five prefixes: أ/ت/ي/ن. Learn the prefix song!","vocab":[{"t":"يدرس","r":"yadrus","en":"he studies","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يعمل","r":"yaʿmal","en":"he works","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يعيش","r":"yaʿīsh","en":"he lives","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يحب","r":"yuḥibb","en":"he loves","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يريد","r":"yurīd","en":"he wants","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يتكلم","r":"yatakallam","en":"he speaks","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يقرأ","r":"yaqraʾ","en":"he reads","pos":"verb"},{"t":"يكتب","r":"yaktub","en":"he writes","pos":"verb"}],"grammar":{"title":"Present prefixes: أ/ت/ي/ن","explain":"أدرس (I study), تدرس (you-m study), يدرس (he studies), تدرس (she studies), ندرس (we study). She and you-m share تـ! Pronouns optional: أدرس alone = I study.","pattern":"أ-/تـ-/يـ-/نـ + stem","examples":[{"t":"أنا أدرس العربية.","r":"anā adrus al-ʿarabiyya.","en":"I study Arabic."},{"t":"هو يتكلم الإنجليزية.","r":"huwa yatakallam al-inglīziyya.","en":"He speaks English."},{"t":"نحن نحب الشاي.","r":"naḥnu nuḥibb ash-shāy.","en":"We love tea."}],"mistakes":["Saying أنا يدرس — I takes أدرس!","Adding أنا every time — أدرس alone is enough!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"ليلى","t":"هل تتكلم الإنجليزية؟","r":"hal tatakallam al-inglīziyya?","en":"Do you speak English? (to m)"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"نعم، أتكلم الإنجليزية. وأنتِ؟","r":"naʿam, atakallam al-inglīziyya. wa anti?","en":"Yes, I speak English. And you? (to f)"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"أنا أدرس العربية!","r":"anā adrus al-ʿarabiyya!","en":"I study Arabic!"},{"sp":"عمر","t":"ممتاز!","r":"mumtāz!","en":"Excellent!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I study Arabic","answer":"أنا أدرس العربية"},{"type":"fill","q":"نحن ___ الشاي. (love)","answer":"نحب"},{"type":"choose","q":"'He speaks English' is…","options":["هو أتكلم الإنجليزية","هو يتكلم الإنجليزية","هو تتكلم الإنجليزية","هو نتكلم الإنجليزية"],"answer":"هو يتكلم الإنجليزية"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: العربية / أدرس / أنا","answer":"أنا أدرس العربية"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: أنا أدرس العربية.","answer":"أنا أدرس العربية."}],"quiz":[{"q":"أدرس means…","options":["you study","I study","he studies","we study"],"answer":1,"why":"أ- = I."},{"q":"يدرس means…","options":["I study","you study","he studies","we study"],"answer":2,"why":"يـ- = he."},{"q":"ندرس means…","options":["I study","you study","he studies","we study"],"answer":3,"why":"نـ- = we."},{"q":"She-studies prefix is…","options":["أ-","يـ-","تـ-","نـ-"],"answer":2,"why":"She shares تـ- with you-m."},{"q":"Pronouns like أنا are…","options":["required","optional","forbidden","plural-only"],"answer":1,"why":"أدرس alone = I study."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Present tense worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["he studies","he loves","he writes"],"key":["يدرس","يحب","يكتب"]},{"instruction":"Conjugate يدرس.","items":["I study","he studies","we study"],"key":["أدرس","يدرس","ندرس"]},{"instruction":"Ask it.","items":["Do you speak English? (to m)","Excellent!"],"key":["هل تتكلم الإنجليزية؟","ممتاز!"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U3-L2","title":"I have: عندي","learn":"عندي = I have (at-me)! عندك (you-m have), عندها (she has). فِي = there is: في البيت (in the house). عندي كتاب = I have a book. Swap endings, own everything!","vocab":[{"t":"عندي","r":"ʿindī","en":"I have","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"في","r":"fī","en":"in / there is","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"خبز","r":"khubz","en":"bread","pos":"noun"},{"t":"ماء","r":"māʾ","en":"water","pos":"noun"},{"t":"بيت","r":"bayt","en":"house","pos":"noun"},{"t":"مال","r":"māl","en":"money","pos":"noun"},{"t":"صديق","r":"ṣadīq","en":"friend","pos":"noun"},{"t":"وقت","r":"waqt","en":"time","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"عندي + thing = I have","explain":"عندي كتاب (I have a book), عندك ماء؟ (do you have water?), ما عندي وقت (I have no time — ما negates!). فِي for places: الكتاب في البيت (the book is in the house).","pattern":"عندي/عندك/عندها + thing · ما… negates","examples":[{"t":"عندي كتاب.","r":"ʿindī kitāb.","en":"I have a book."},{"t":"عندك ماء؟","r":"ʿindak māʾ?","en":"Do you have water? (m)"},{"t":"ما عندي وقت.","r":"mā ʿindī waqt.","en":"I have no time."}],"mistakes":["Saying أنا أملك first — natives say عندي!","Saying لا عندي — negate with ما: ما عندي!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"عمر","t":"عندك ماء؟","r":"ʿindak māʾ?","en":"Do you have water? (to m)"},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"نعم، عندي ماء وخبز.","r":"naʿam, ʿindī māʾ wa khubz.","en":"Yes, I have water and bread."},{"sp":"عمر","t":"شكرا! ما عندي مال.","r":"shukran! mā ʿindī māl.","en":"Thanks! I have no money."},{"sp":"ليلى","t":"عفوا!","r":"ʿafwan!","en":"You're welcome!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I have a book","answer":"عندي كتاب"},{"type":"fill","q":"ما عندي ___. (time)","answer":"وقت"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Do you have water?' (to m) is…","options":["هل تريد ماء؟","عندك ماء؟","أين الماء؟","هل تشرب ماء؟"],"answer":"عندك ماء؟"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: كتاب / عندي","answer":"عندي كتاب"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: عندي ماء وخبز.","answer":"عندي ماء وخبز."}],"quiz":[{"q":"عندي كتاب means…","options":["I want a book","I have a book","I read a book","I see a book"],"answer":1,"why":"عندي = I have."},{"q":"Negate with…","options":["لا","ما","لم","لن"],"answer":1,"why":"ما عندي = I don't have."},{"q":"مال means…","options":["books","money","bread","water"],"answer":1,"why":"مال = money."},{"q":"عندك ماء؟ means…","options":["Are you here?","Do you have water?","Do you want?","Where is water?"],"answer":1,"why":"عندك = you have (m)."},{"q":"خبز means…","options":["water","bread","house","friend"],"answer":1,"why":"خبز = bread."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"I have worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Arabic.","items":["I have","money","time"],"key":["عندي","مال","وقت"]},{"instruction":"Have things.","items":["I have a book","Do you have water? (m)","I have no time"],"key":["عندي كتاب","عندك ماء؟","ما عندي وقت"]},{"instruction":"At the table.","items":["I have water and bread","I have no money"],"key":["عندي ماء وخبز","ما عندي مال"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Peace upon you!","answer":"السلام عليكم!"},{"type":"fill","q":"صباح ___! (morning reply)","answer":"النور"},{"type":"choose","q":"Reply to السلام عليكم","options":["السلام عليكم","وعليكم السلام","صباح الخير","مع السلامة"],"answer":"وعليكم السلام"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I study Arabic","answer":"أنا أدرس العربية"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"عندي ماء.","answer":"I have water."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ مدرسة. (This, f)","answer":"هذه"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: ليلى / اسمي","answer":"اسمي ليلى"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: أنا أدرس العربية.","answer":"أنا أدرس العربية."},{"type":"fill","q":"ما عندي ___. (time)","answer":"وقت"},{"type":"choose","q":"هو يتكلم الإنجليزية.","options":["I speak English","He speaks English","We speak English","You speak English"],"answer":"He speaks English"}]}}}